@startuml
!theme plain
left to right direction
title FleetIQ Guardian - Deck-Friendly Solution Flow

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #19226D
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

rectangle "1. Inputs\n\nRoad cameras\nDriver camera\nSensor fusion" as Inputs #EAF2FF
rectangle "2. Per-source Models\n\nRoad context\nDriver state\nVehicle state" as Models #FFFFFF
rectangle "3. Aligned Feature Windows\n\n1-5s timeline vectors\nconfidence + missing flags" as Vectors #FFF7EE
rectangle "4. Risk Intelligence\n\nTTC + lane + driver fusion\nlearned risk detector" as Risk #F37021
rectangle "5. Fleet Outputs\n\nTrip score\nEvent evidence\nCoaching report\nDashboard" as Outputs #EAF2FF

Inputs --> Models
Models --> Vectors
Vectors --> Risk
Risk --> Outputs

rectangle "Verified Model Training\n\nground truth + precise rules\nhuman-reviewed labels\ntrain calibrated model" as Training #F7F8FB
Vectors --> Training : sampled windows
Training --> Risk : model version

rectangle "Post-Inference Risk Discovery\n\nrisk embeddings -> clustering\nLLM names completed clusters\nanalytics metadata only" as Discovery #F7F8FB
Risk --> Discovery : risk outputs
Discovery --> Outputs : cluster labels

note bottom of Risk
Online detector is a trained lightweight model.
LLM only names post-inference clusters.
LLM output is never used for model training.
end note

@enduml
